{"id": "samsung_elec-2026-09-23-009", "date": "2026-09-23", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 39, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": ["samsung_elec", "lg_elec"], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["panel_price", "oled_penetration"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.7, "reasons": ["多公司提及"]}, "title": "India investigates LG and Samsung as both companies are suspected to pay lower tariff on imported OLED TV panels", "content": "<p>According to <a href=\"https://www.reuters.com/business/media-telecom/lg-samsung-face-india-tariff-evasion-investigation-over-oled-tv-parts-2026-09-23/\">Reuters</a>, the Indian government is investigating LG Electronics and Samsung Electronics, as it is suspected that the two companies paid lower tariffs on imported OLED TV panels. These panels were later assembled into TVs in India.&nbsp;</p><div class=\"align-center\">\n  \n  <a href=\"https://www.oled-info.com/sites/default/files/2026-01/LG-OLED", "sources": [{"name": "oled_info", "url": "https://www.oled-info.com/india-investigates-lg-and-samsung-both-companies-are-suspected-pay-lower-tariff", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-23-010", "date": "2026-09-23", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 39, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["oled_penetration"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Researchers develop photoresistive polymer OLED devices based on the core-shell principle", "content": "<p>Researchers from ETH Zurich, in collaboration with researchers from RMIT University in Melbourne, developed polymer OLED emitters, that can also serve as photoresists - which means that these materials can be precisely patterned using photolithography. This could open the door to the production of ultra-fine polymer OLED devices.&nbsp;</p><div>\n  \n  <a href=\"https://www.oled-info.com/sites/default/files/2026-09/ETH-Zurich-photoresistive-polymer-OLED-structure.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">\n    \n    <i", "sources": [{"name": "oled_info", "url": "https://www.oled-info.com/researchers-develop-photoresistive-polymer-oled-devices-based-core-shell", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-23-011", "date": "2026-09-23", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 39, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["automotive_display"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["growth"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Automotive display growth shifts to HUDs, passenger screens", "content": "<p class=\"P1\" data-start=\"2789\" data-end=\"3284\">The global automotive display market is entering a new phase of growth, with demand shifting away from central consoles and instrument clusters toward niche applications such as head-up displays (HUDs) and front-passenger entertainment panels. DIGITIMES Intelligence analyst Jason Yang said the global automotive display shipment compound annual growth rate (CAGR) is expected to reach only about 2.4% from 2026 to 2031, but HUDs and entertainment pane", "sources": [{"name": "digitimes_display", "url": "https://www.digitimes.com/news/a20260922PD241/growth-automotive-display-display-panel-market.html", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "lg_elec-2026-09-23-012", "date": "2026-09-23", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 39, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": ["lg_elec"], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": [], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "LG Electronics, Microsoft enter partnership on AI data centers, physical AI", "content": "LG Electronics entered a partnership with Microsoft to cooperate on a range of AI initiatives. The two firms agreed to work together on AI data centers, LG Electronics' AI data transformation, and physical AI as the company known for appliances taps into growing AI-related industries.", "sources": [{"name": "digitimes_display", "url": "https://www.digitimes.com/news/a20260923VL215/microsoft-lg-electronics-partnership-data-lg.html", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "samsung_elec-2026-09-23-013", "date": "2026-09-23", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 39, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": ["samsung_elec"], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["oled_penetration"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Samsung Display explores halftone black PDL tech to cut OLED production costs", "content": "<p class=\"P1\" data-start=\"2236\" data-end=\"2640\">Samsung Display is evaluating a new manufacturing process known as halftone black pixel definition layer (PDL) that could streamline the production of its OLED panels, industry sources disclosed to <em data-start=\"2434\" data-end=\"2444\">The ELEC</em> on September 22. By integrating two separate manufacturing steps into a single photolithography process, the display maker aims to reduce costs and boost efficiency for upcoming flagship devices.", "sources": [{"name": "digitimes_display", "url": "https://www.digitimes.com/news/a20260923VL214/sdc-production-manufacturing-flagship-samsung.html", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-23-014", "date": "2026-09-23", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 39, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["earnings"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.75, "reasons": ["涉及財報"]}, "title": "Hermes-Epitek eyes CPO test revenue in 2027", "content": "<p class=\"P1\" data-start=\"3600\" data-end=\"3906\">Archie Hwang, the founder and chairman of Hermes-Epitek, appeared before the media alongside Hermes Testing Solutions Inc. (HTSI) executives. The company outlined a major push into silicon photonics (SiPh) co-packaged optics (CPO) testing and said related revenue is expected to begin contributing in 2027.", "sources": [{"name": "digitimes_display", "url": "https://www.digitimes.com/news/a20260923PD223/chairman-cpo-revenue-2027-testing.html", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "lg_elec-2026-09-23-015", "date": "2026-09-23", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 39, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": ["lg_elec"], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": [], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "LG Energy enters Nvidia's ecosystem as it pivots batteries to data centers", "content": "LG Energy's battery energy storage system (BESS) has entered Nvidia's AI Factory ecosystem. Its qualification by the chipmaker comes as LG Energy is reorienting its North American battery plants toward data centers and appears poised to capture fresh demand after the US imposed restrictions on Chinese battery imports.", "sources": [{"name": "digitimes_display", "url": "https://www.digitimes.com/news/a20260923VL213/lg-nvidia-data-market-certification.html", "type": "rss"}]}
